<title>SPAIN: Heavy rains damage grain crops in northern Spain.</title>
<headline>Heavy rains damage grain crops in northern Spain.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heavy rains in north-central Spain, the country's main grain-producing region, have caused significant property and crop damage and the area remains on alert for possible further rainfall, a Civil Guard official told Reuters on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;I have just received a fax from the regional government of Palencia and damage is really significant and they will declare the area a disaster zone,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>No further details were immediately available.</p>
<p>In Palencia, a region within northern Castille-Leon, 103 litres per square metre of rain had fallen in storms, causing widespread damage to buildings, infrastructure, electrical network and roads.</p>
<p>But crops were hit the worst. Grains and fruits were severely affected as rivers overflowed their banks and flooded fields, she said.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
